msgid "Part 5 — Extending the Package"
msgstr "Partie 5 — Étendre le paquet"

msgid ""
"This part is for developers who write their own class on top of **ndict-"
"tools**. It explains what to subclass, how a subclass sets its "
"configuration, and what it inherits without writing anything."
msgstr ""
"Cette partie s’adresse aux développeurs qui écrivent leur propre classe "
"au-dessus de **ndict-tools**. Elle explique de quoi hériter, comment une "
"sous-classe définit sa configuration, et ce dont elle hérite sans rien "
"écrire."

msgid "Public and private classes"
msgstr "Classes publiques et classes privées"

msgid "The package has a private engine and a public interface:"
msgstr "Le paquet a un moteur privé et une interface publique :"

msgid ""
"ndict_tools/\n"
"├── tools.py      ← private engine   (_StackedDict, _HKey, _Paths, "
"_CPaths)\n"
"├── core.py       ← public classes   (NestedDictionary, PathsView, …)\n"
"├── serialize.py  ← private helpers  (JSON key encoding, pickle checks)\n"
"├── exception.py  ← exceptions\n"
"└── __init__.py   ← exports the public classes and the exceptions"
msgstr ""
"ndict_tools/\n"
"├── tools.py      ← moteur privé       (_StackedDict, _HKey, _Paths, "
"_CPaths)\n"
"├── core.py       ← classes publiques  (NestedDictionary, PathsView, …)\n"
"├── serialize.py  ← outils privés      (encodage des clés JSON, contrôles"
" pickle)\n"
"├── exception.py  ← exceptions\n"
"└── __init__.py   ← exporte les classes publiques et les exceptions"

msgid ""
"``__init__.py`` exports the classes of ``core.py`` and the exceptions, "
"and nothing from ``tools.py`` or ``serialize.py``. Subclass the public "
"classes, usually :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, never the "
"private ones: the private classes can change between releases. Their "
"reference is in :doc:`/api/internal/tools` and "
":doc:`/api/internal/serialize`."
msgstr ""
"``__init__.py`` exporte les classes de ``core.py`` et les exceptions, et "
"rien de ``tools.py`` ni de ``serialize.py``. Héritez des classes "
"publiques, en général de :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, jamais "
"des classes privées : celles-ci peuvent changer d’une version à l’autre. "
"Leur référence se trouve dans :doc:`/api/internal/tools` et "
":doc:`/api/internal/serialize`."

msgid "The configuration of a subclass"
msgstr "La configuration d’une sous-classe"

msgid ""
"The configuration of a nested dictionary, its ``default_setup``, is what "
"every level of the dictionary shares: ``indent`` and ``default_factory`` "
"for the public classes. A subclass extends the package by adding its own "
"setting to it, which then follows the dictionary everywhere the "
"configuration goes."
msgstr ""
"La configuration d’un dictionnaire imbriqué, son ``default_setup``, est "
"ce que partagent tous les niveaux du dictionnaire : ``indent`` et "
"``default_factory`` pour les classes publiques. Une sous-classe étend le "
"paquet en y ajoutant son propre réglage, qui suit alors le dictionnaire "
"partout où va la configuration."

msgid ""
"Every way of building an instance resolves the configuration through one "
"class method, ``_normalize_setup``: the constructor, the "
"``default_setup`` setter, :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict`"
" and :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_json`. It receives the "
"``default_setup`` given by the caller, or ``None``, and returns the "
"configuration to apply as a new :class:`dict`, without changing the one "
"it received. :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` supplies its default "
"there; :class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` and "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` force their "
"``default_factory`` there."
msgstr ""
"Toutes les façons de construire une instance résolvent la configuration "
"par une seule méthode de classe, ``_normalize_setup`` : le constructeur, "
"le setter de ``default_setup``, "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict` et "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_json`. Elle reçoit le "
"``default_setup`` fourni par l’appelant, ou ``None``, et renvoie la "
"configuration à appliquer sous forme de nouveau :class:`dict`, sans "
"modifier celui qu’elle a reçu. :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` y "
"fournit sa configuration par défaut ; "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` et "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` y imposent leur "
"``default_factory``."

msgid ""
"Here is an ``Inventory`` of a house whose configuration also holds the "
"unit in which powers are given:"
msgstr ""
"Voici un ``Inventory`` de maison dont la configuration contient aussi "
"l’unité dans laquelle les puissances sont exprimées :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> class Inventory(NestedDictionary):\n"
"...     \"\"\"A nested dictionary describing the equipment of a "
"house.\"\"\"\n"
"...\n"
"...     def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n"
"...         self.unit: str = \"W\"\n"
"...         super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)\n"
"...\n"
"...     @classmethod\n"
"...     def _normalize_setup(cls, setup):\n"
"...         normalized = dict(setup) if setup else {\"indent\": 2, "
"\"default_factory\": cls}\n"
"...         normalized.setdefault(\"unit\", \"W\")\n"
"...         return super()._normalize_setup(normalized)\n"
"...\n"
"...     def total_power(self):\n"
"...         total = sum(value for path, value in self.unpacked_items() if"
" path[-1] == \"power\")\n"
"...         return f\"{total} {self.unit}\""
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> class Inventory(NestedDictionary):\n"
"...     \"\"\"A nested dictionary describing the equipment of a "
"house.\"\"\"\n"
"...\n"
"...     def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n"
"...         self.unit: str = \"W\"\n"
"...         super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)\n"
"...\n"
"...     @classmethod\n"
"...     def _normalize_setup(cls, setup):\n"
"...         normalized = dict(setup) if setup else {\"indent\": 2, "
"\"default_factory\": cls}\n"
"...         normalized.setdefault(\"unit\", \"W\")\n"
"...         return super()._normalize_setup(normalized)\n"
"...\n"
"...     def total_power(self):\n"
"...         total = sum(value for path, value in self.unpacked_items() if"
" path[-1] == \"power\")\n"
"...         return f\"{total} {self.unit}\""

msgid "The two methods have separate jobs:"
msgstr "Les deux méthodes ont des rôles distincts :"

msgid ""
"``__init__`` declares ``unit`` as an attribute of the instance, before "
"calling the parent constructor, as :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`"
" does for ``indent``. The parent constructor then applies the "
"configuration, and it only accepts keys that are attributes of the "
"instance: without this declaration, ``unit`` would raise "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StackedAttributeError`."
msgstr ""
"``__init__`` déclare ``unit`` comme attribut de l’instance, avant "
"d’appeler le constructeur parent, comme "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` le fait pour ``indent``. Le "
"constructeur parent applique ensuite la configuration, et il n’accepte "
"que des clés qui sont des attributs de l’instance : sans cette "
"déclaration, ``unit`` lèverait une "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StackedAttributeError`."

msgid ""
"``_normalize_setup`` gives the default configuration, completes a "
"configuration that has no ``unit``, and hands the result to the parent "
"class, which checks that ``indent`` and ``default_factory`` are present."
msgstr ""
"``_normalize_setup`` donne la configuration par défaut, complète une "
"configuration qui n’a pas de ``unit``, et transmet le résultat à la "
"classe parente, qui vérifie la présence de ``indent`` et de "
"``default_factory``."

msgid "Four rules follow."
msgstr "Quatre règles en découlent."

msgid ""
"**1. A new setting is an instance attribute and a configuration key.** "
"The constructor sets it on every level, like ``indent``. A house measured"
" in kilowatts:"
msgstr ""
"**1. Un nouveau réglage est un attribut d’instance et une clé de "
"configuration.** Le constructeur le définit à chaque niveau, comme "
"``indent``. Une maison mesurée en kilowatts :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> house = Inventory(\n"
"...     {\n"
"...         \"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": "
"{\"type\": \"radiator\", \"power\": 1.5}},\n"
"...         \"bedroom\": {\"heating\": {\"type\": \"radiator\", "
"\"power\": 1.0}},\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": Inventory, "
"\"unit\": \"kW\"},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> house.unit, house[\"kitchen\"].unit, house[[\"kitchen\", "
"\"heating\"]].unit\n"
"('kW', 'kW', 'kW')\n"
">>> house.total_power()\n"
"'2.5 kW'\n"
">>> house[\"bedroom\"].total_power()\n"
"'1.0 kW'"
msgstr ""
">>> house = Inventory(\n"
"...     {\n"
"...         \"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": "
"{\"type\": \"radiator\", \"power\": 1.5}},\n"
"...         \"bedroom\": {\"heating\": {\"type\": \"radiator\", "
"\"power\": 1.0}},\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": Inventory, "
"\"unit\": \"kW\"},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> house.unit, house[\"kitchen\"].unit, house[[\"kitchen\", "
"\"heating\"]].unit\n"
"('kW', 'kW', 'kW')\n"
">>> house.total_power()\n"
"'2.5 kW'\n"
">>> house[\"bedroom\"].total_power()\n"
"'1.0 kW'"

msgid ""
"Assigning ``default_setup`` later changes the setting at every level, as "
"Part 1 shows for ``indent``."
msgstr ""
"Affecter ``default_setup`` plus tard modifie le réglage à tous les "
"niveaux, comme le montre la partie 1 pour ``indent``."

msgid ""
"**2. Define the default, or always pass it.** Without ``default_setup``, "
"an ``Inventory`` gets the configuration of ``_normalize_setup``, in "
"watts:"
msgstr ""
"**2. Définissez la valeur par défaut, ou fournissez-la toujours.** Sans "
"``default_setup``, un ``Inventory`` reçoit la configuration de "
"``_normalize_setup``, en watts :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> Inventory({\"office\": {\"heating\": {\"power\": "
"500}}}).total_power()\n"
"'500 W'"
msgstr ""
">>> Inventory({\"office\": {\"heating\": {\"power\": "
"500}}}).total_power()\n"
"'500 W'"

msgid ""
"A subclass that does not override ``_normalize_setup`` inherits the "
"default of its parent, which has no ``unit``."
msgstr ""
"Une sous-classe qui ne redéfinit pas ``_normalize_setup`` hérite de la "
"valeur par défaut de son parent, qui n’a pas de ``unit``."

msgid ""
"**3. Use the subclass as its own** ``default_factory``. The nested "
"dictionaries given to the constructor or to ``from_dict`` are converted "
"with the class that builds them. Keys created by reading a missing key, "
"however, come from ``default_factory``. The default above uses ``cls``, "
"so both kinds of levels are ``Inventory`` objects, and so are those of a "
"subclass of ``Inventory``:"
msgstr ""
"**3. Faites de la sous-classe son propre** ``default_factory``. Les "
"dictionnaires imbriqués passés au constructeur ou à ``from_dict`` sont "
"convertis avec la classe qui les construit. Les clés créées par la "
"lecture d’une clé absente, en revanche, viennent de ``default_factory``. "
"La valeur par défaut ci-dessus utilise ``cls`` ; les deux sortes de "
"niveaux sont donc des objets ``Inventory``, et il en va de même pour une "
"sous-classe de ``Inventory`` :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> home = Inventory({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> type(home[\"kitchen\"]).__name__\n"
"'Inventory'\n"
">>> type(home[\"attic\"]).__name__\n"
"'Inventory'"
msgstr ""
">>> home = Inventory({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> type(home[\"kitchen\"]).__name__\n"
"'Inventory'\n"
">>> type(home[\"attic\"]).__name__\n"
"'Inventory'"

msgid ""
"Without this, the two kinds of levels differ. A bare subclass keeps the "
"``default_factory`` of :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`:"
msgstr ""
"Sans cela, les deux sortes de niveaux diffèrent. Une sous-classe nue "
"conserve le réglage ``default_factory`` de "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> class BareInventory(NestedDictionary):\n"
"...     pass\n"
">>> bare = BareInventory({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> type(bare[\"kitchen\"]).__name__\n"
"'BareInventory'\n"
">>> type(bare[\"attic\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'"
msgstr ""
">>> class BareInventory(NestedDictionary):\n"
"...     pass\n"
">>> bare = BareInventory({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> type(bare[\"kitchen\"]).__name__\n"
"'BareInventory'\n"
">>> type(bare[\"attic\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'"

msgid ""
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` follows the same rule: its "
"``_normalize_setup`` sets ``default_factory`` to itself."
msgstr ""
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` suit la même règle : sa "
"méthode ``_normalize_setup`` règle ``default_factory`` sur elle-même."

msgid ""
"**4. The other constructors need no override.** "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict`, "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.copy` and "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.deepcopy` build through the class of"
" the instance and keep its configuration, ``unit`` included:"
msgstr ""
"**4. Les autres constructeurs n’ont pas besoin d’être redéfinis.** "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict`, "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.copy` et "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.deepcopy` construisent avec la "
"classe de l’instance et conservent sa configuration, ``unit`` compris :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> kilowatts = {\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": Inventory, \"unit\":"
" \"kW\"}\n"
">>> Inventory.from_dict({\"garage\": {\"charger\": {\"power\": 7.4}}}, "
"default_setup=kilowatts).total_power()\n"
"'7.4 kW'\n"
">>> copied = house.deepcopy()\n"
">>> type(copied).__name__, copied.unit, copied == house\n"
"('Inventory', 'kW', True)"
msgstr ""
">>> kilowatts = {\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": Inventory, \"unit\":"
" \"kW\"}\n"
">>> Inventory.from_dict({\"garage\": {\"charger\": {\"power\": 7.4}}}, "
"default_setup=kilowatts).total_power()\n"
"'7.4 kW'\n"
">>> copied = house.deepcopy()\n"
">>> type(copied).__name__, copied.unit, copied == house\n"
"('Inventory', 'kW', True)"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_pickle` returns the object with"
" the configuration it had when written. Pickle stores the class by its "
"name, so a subclass that is pickled must be defined at the top level of "
"an importable module. A JSON file holds the content only (see "
":doc:`serialization`): :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_json` "
"returns an ``Inventory`` with the default configuration, in watts, unless"
" ``default_setup`` is given."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_pickle` renvoie l’objet avec la"
" configuration qu’il avait lors de son écriture. Pickle enregistre la "
"classe par son nom ; une sous-classe enregistrée avec pickle doit donc "
"être définie au premier niveau d’un module importable. Un fichier JSON ne"
" contient que le contenu (voir :doc:`serialization`) : "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_json` renvoie un ``Inventory`` "
"avec la configuration par défaut, en watts, sauf si ``default_setup`` est"
" fourni."

msgid ""
">>> house.to_json(\"house.json\")\n"
">>> Inventory.from_json(\"house.json\").unit\n"
"'W'\n"
">>> Inventory.from_json(\"house.json\", "
"default_setup=kilowatts).total_power()\n"
"'2.5 kW'"
msgstr ""
">>> house.to_json(\"house.json\")\n"
">>> Inventory.from_json(\"house.json\").unit\n"
"'W'\n"
">>> Inventory.from_json(\"house.json\", "
"default_setup=kilowatts).total_power()\n"
"'2.5 kW'"

msgid ""
"Since ``unit`` is part of the configuration, it also counts in "
"comparisons (see :doc:`exploring`): the same content with another unit is"
" isomorphic, not equal."
msgstr ""
"Comme ``unit`` fait partie de la configuration, il compte aussi dans les "
"comparaisons (voir :doc:`exploring`) : le même contenu avec une autre "
"unité est isomorphe, mais pas égal."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> watts = {\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": Inventory, \"unit\": "
"\"W\"}\n"
">>> in_watts = Inventory(house.to_dict(), default_setup=watts)\n"
">>> in_watts == house, in_watts.isomorph(house)\n"
"(False, True)"
msgstr ""
">>> watts = {\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": Inventory, \"unit\": "
"\"W\"}\n"
">>> in_watts = Inventory(house.to_dict(), default_setup=watts)\n"
">>> in_watts == house, in_watts.isomorph(house)\n"
"(False, True)"

msgid "Where the model is described"
msgstr "Où le modèle est décrit"

msgid ""
"The guide only covers the public interface. How the keys of a nested "
"dictionary form a forest, what its paths and compact paths are, and how "
"coverage is computed are explained in the :doc:`/concepts/index` section."
" The private classes that implement them are documented in the API "
"reference."
msgstr ""
"Le guide ne couvre que l’interface publique. La façon dont les clés d’un "
"dictionnaire imbriqué forment une forêt, ce que sont ses chemins et ses "
"chemins compacts, et la manière dont la couverture est calculée sont "
"expliqués dans la section :doc:`/concepts/index`. Les classes privées qui"
" les implémentent sont documentées dans la référence de l’API."

